Rules for JSON:
- source = caller, target = callee.
- call_count: use number of distinct call sites if unknown (not fake traffic).
- avg_latency_ms and error_rate: 0 unless you have real metrics (do not invent).
- confidence high = explicit client/URL/proto; medium = env name / helm; low = string match on service name.
- Prefer fewer high-confidence edges over a hairball of low-confidence ones.
- layer must be inferred from the graph (edge = nothing calls it, infra = many callers or db/auth, etc.), not from a generic template.
- If this workspace is one service, still list outbound dependencies as targets (other services/infra), and say in meta that other repos were not in the workspace.

If multiple services are missing because they live in other repos, list those repo names under meta.notes so we can clone them next.

